 CODE
2.3.25. 
Common debts 
The following are common debts 
1¡ debts contracted jointly or severally by the two spouses; 
2¡ debts contracted by one of the spouses for the needs of the household and the education of the children; 
3¡ debts contracted by one of the spouses in the interest of the common patrimony; 
4¡ debts on gifts made to both spouses jointly or to one of them with the stipulation that the property given or bequeathed will be common; 
5¡ interest on debts belonging to one of the spouses; 
6¡ maintenance debts in favour of the descendants of one of the spouses.
Debts which are not proved to be the property of one of the spouses by application of a provision of the law are also joint.
